From: pulpoff <pashkovsky@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] monitor: Allow a phone's logical size

A scale is valid only if the logical monitor it leaves is at least
600 x 600 in area. The S10e's 1080 x 2280 panel at scale 3, Android's own
3 px per dp, is 360 x 760: under that, so mutter refused it and the
phone ran at 2.5, every GNOME app at 0.83 of Android's size. Allow down
to 360 x 640, the smallest logical screen GNOME's adaptive apps are
built for (libadwaita's 360 px minimum width).

For mutter-mobile 51.1.mobile.22 (/usr/src/gnome-mobile/mutter on the
S10e, built into /opt/gnome-mobile by build51.sh).
---
--- a/src/backends/meta-monitor.c
+++ b/src/backends/meta-monitor.c
@@ -33,7 +33,7 @@
 #define MAX_DENOMINATOR 4
 #define MIN_INTEGER_SCALE 1
 #define MAX_INTEGER_SCALE 4
-#define MINIMUM_LOGICAL_AREA (600 * 600)
+#define MINIMUM_LOGICAL_AREA (360 * 640)
 #define MAXIMUM_REFRESH_RATE_DIFF 0.001f
 
 typedef struct _MetaMonitorModePrivate
